/**
 * PANCREATIC CANCER: THE UK AND NHS LAYER. Facts checked 2026-09-24 against the pages cited on each row.
 *
 * What is here: the UK figures by nation (Cancer Research UK on the four registries; Public Health Scotland's open data
 * CSV, the Welsh Cancer Intelligence and Surveillance Unit's count, stage and mortality spreadsheets and the Northern
 * Ireland Cancer Registry's tables, each read from its own download; NDRS pages answered 403), the National Pancreatic
 * Cancer Audit's 2026 State of the Nation report with its headline findings and dates, the NHS route from the NG12
 * referral rules (including the over-60 weight loss with new-onset diabetes rule) through the 28, 31 and 62 day standards,
 * the specialist HPB MDT and the 23 English surgical hubs, Pancreatic Cancer UK's Optimal Care Pathway, PERT, dietetic
 * and diabetes input and germline testing; every NICE decision on a pancreatic cancer medicine, verified on nice.org.uk
 * (one recommendation, one refusal, two terminated appraisals), NG85's chemotherapy recommendations and the SMC's four
 * decisions; the tests a patient can ask about; the UK trials open with their ISRCTN sites; the UK trial legacy (ESPAC,
 * EUROPAC, Precision-Panc); UK researchers from their public university pages; the charities, the costs and the benefits;
 * and where the four nations differ. No figure is remembered: each carries the page it was read from. Where a page could
 * not be read, the gap is named with the response the server gave.
 *
 * The cancer record is `pancreatic` (src/data/cancers.ts, "Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma"); the resectability and
 * molecular subtype records in src/data/pancreatic-subtypes.ts are aliases. This file adds the HPB units the gallbladder
 * pass did not record (Hull, Stoke, Coventry, Guildford, Blackburn, Dundee, Aberdeen, Inverness), the two pancreatic
 * charities, the Glasgow research centre, five researchers, the EUROPAC and Precision-Panc records, and the `ukPathway`.
 */
